{
  // Scoped override of the root deno.json's "exclude": ["apps", ...]. That
  // exclude is deliberate (a bare `deno test`/`deno lint` at repo root should
  // not wander into apps/ or packages/, which are npm/React/Vite, not Deno) —
  // but Deno's exclude also blocks explicit paths under an excluded directory
  // (contrary to the root file's own comment; verified empirically:
  // `deno test apps/mobile/tests-deno/` from the REPO ROOT reports "No test
  // modules found" without this file).
  //
  // Deno resolves the nearest deno.json starting from the PROCESS'S CWD, not
  // from the target path argument — so this override only takes effect when
  // Deno is actually invoked from inside this directory:
  //
  //   cd apps/mobile/tests-deno && deno test .
  //
  // Running `deno test apps/mobile/tests-deno/` from the repo root still hits
  // the root config's exclude and reports no test modules, even with this
  // file present. This file's job is just to make `deno test .` work with no
  // extra flags once you're standing in this directory; it does not change
  // discovery from elsewhere.
}
